    "html": "<html lang=\"en\"><head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n    <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\">\n    <title>FABRIK Algorithm (2D) [sean.fun]</title>\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,minimum-scale=1\">\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"FABRIK stands for Forward-and-Backward Reaching Inverse Kinematics, and it’s a very simple, fast, and clever solution to the inverse kinematics problem. Let’s inspect this interesting algorithm in 2D.\">\n    <meta name=\"generator\" content=\"Hugo 0.138.0\">\n    <meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow\">\n    <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/favicon.png\" type=\"image/png\">\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/style.min.a936baa10ffe9ca9af7623184f7b88dd1084c740bb2758a8213343f97c917598.css\">\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" href=\"https://sean.fun/a/fabrik-algorithm-2d/rss.xml\" title=\"sean.fun\">\n    <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://sean.fun/a/fabrik-algorithm-2d/\">\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin=\"\"><link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" href=\"https://sean.fun/a/fabrik-algorithm-2d/rss.xml\" title=\"sean.fun\">\n    <meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"sean.fun\">\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"FABRIK Algorithm (2D)\">\n    <meta itemprop=\"name\" content=\"FABRIK Algorithm (2D)\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"FABRIK Algorithm (2D)\">\n    <meta itemprop=\"description\" content=\"The [FABRIK algorithm](/a/fabrik-algorithm-2d) is an amazingly clever solution to the Inverse Kinematics problem – how to adjust the joints of an arm to reach a target location.  In this tutorial, I go over how the core algorithm works in 2D, building up from simple concepts.\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"The [FABRIK algorithm](/a/fabrik-algorithm-2d) is an amazingly clever solution to the Inverse Kinematics problem – how to adjust the joints of an arm to reach a target location.  In this tutorial, I go over how the core algorithm works in 2D, building up from simple concepts.\">\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"The [FABRIK algorithm](/a/fabrik-algorithm-2d) is an amazingly clever solution to the Inverse Kinematics problem – how to adjust the joints of an arm to reach a target location.  In this tutorial, I go over how the core algorithm works in 2D, building up from simple concepts.\">\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\">\n    <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://sean.fun/a/fabrik-algorithm-2d/\">\n    <meta itemprop=\"wordCount\" content=\"1024\">\n    <meta itemprop=\"keywords\" content=\"2d, algorithm, javascript, heuristic\">\n    <meta property=\"article:section\" content=\"article\">\n    <meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2018-01-09T00:00:00+00:00\">\n    <meta itemprop=\"datePublished\" content=\"2018-01-09T00:00:00+00:00\">\n    <meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2018-01-09T00:00:00+00:00\">\n    <meta itemprop=\"dateModified\" content=\"2018-01-09T00:00:00+00:00\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://sean.fun/who/me.jpg\">\n    <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://sean.fun/who/me.jpg\">\n    <meta itemprop=\"image\" content=\"https://sean.fun/who/me.jpg\">\n  </head>\n  <body id=\"top\">\n    <nav class=\"site mobile\">\n      <button type=\"button\" onclick=\"javascript: { const s = 'mobile-menu-fade-'; const o = ['out', 'in']; const b = document.getElementById('mobile-menu'); if (b.classList.contains(s + o[1])) o.push(o.shift()); b.classList.remove(s + o[0]);b.classList.add(s + o[1]); }\">\n        <svg width=\"40\" height=\"40\" viewBox=\"0 0 40 40\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n          <path d=\"M5,11 H30 M5,20 H30 M5,29 H30\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"></path>\n        </svg>\n      </button>\n      <a href=\"/\"><img class=\"logo\" src=\"/logo.png\" alt=\"Logo\"></a>\n    </nav>\n    <nav class=\"site\" id=\"mobile-menu\">\n      <div>\n  <h2>Home</h2>\n  <ol>\n    <li><a href=\"/\">Welcome</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/who\">About Me</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/store\">Store</a></li>\n  </ol>\n</div>\n<div>\n  <h2>Creations</h2>\n  <ol>\n    <li><a href=\"/games\">Games</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/velipso\" target=\"_blank\">Music</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/wood\">Woodworking</a></li>\n  </ol>\n</div>\n<div>\n  <h2>Programming</h2>\n  <ol>\n    <li><a href=\"/tutorials\">Tutorials</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/software\">Software</a></li>\n  </ol>\n</div>\n<div>\n  <h2>Weird Stuff</h2>\n  <ol>\n    <li><a href=\"/out-of-body\">Out of Body</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/experiments\">Experiments</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/maybe\">Hypotheticals</a></li>\n  </ol>\n</div>\n\n    </nav>\n    <div id=\"wrapper\">\n      <nav class=\"site desktop\">\n        <a href=\"/\"><img class=\"logo\" src=\"/logo.png\" alt=\"Logo\"></a>\n        <div>\n  <h2>Home</h2>\n  <ol>\n    <li><a href=\"/\">Welcome</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/who\">About Me</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/store\">Store</a></li>\n  </ol>\n</div>\n<div>\n  <h2>Creations</h2>\n  <ol>\n    <li><a href=\"/games\">Games</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/velipso\" target=\"_blank\">Music</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/wood\">Woodworking</a></li>\n  </ol>\n</div>\n<div>\n  <h2>Programming</h2>\n  <ol>\n    <li><a href=\"/tutorials\">Tutorials</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/software\">Software</a></li>\n  </ol>\n</div>\n<div>\n  <h2>Weird Stuff</h2>\n  <ol>\n    <li><a href=\"/out-of-body\">Out of Body</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/experiments\">Experiments</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/maybe\">Hypotheticals</a></li>\n  </ol>\n</div>\n\n      </nav>\n      <main role=\"main\"><article>\n    <h2 class=\"head\">\n      <time datetime=\"2018-01-09T00:00:00Z\">Jan 9, 2018</time>\n      <a href=\"/t/2d/\">2d,</a>\n      <a href=\"/t/algorithm/\">Algorithm,</a>\n      <a href=\"/t/javascript/\">Javascript</a></h2>\n    <h1 class=\"title\">FABRIK Algorithm (2D)</h1><p><a href=\"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1524070311000178?via%3Dihub\">FABRIK</a> stands for\nForward-and-Backward Reaching Inverse Kinematics, and it’s a very simple, fast, and clever solution\nto the inverse kinematics problem.</p>\n<p>Let’s inspect this interesting algorithm in 2D.</p>\n<h2 id=\"problem\">Problem</h2>\n<p>First of all, what is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inverse_kinematics\">Inverse Kinematics</a> (IK)?</p>\n<p>Suppose you have a robotic arm with three joints, whose job is to point to a location:</p>\n<div class=\"img flat\">\n  <canvas id=\"cnv1\" width=\"1200\" height=\"600\" style=\"width: 600px; height: auto;\"></canvas><p>Simplified Robot Arm</p></div>\n\n<script>\nfunction mousepos(e){\n  return [\n    Math.round(e.offsetX * e.target.width / e.target.clientWidth),\n    Math.round(e.offsetY * e.target.width / e.target.clientWidth)\n  ];\n}\nfunction drawX(ctx, p, scale){\n  var sz = Math.round(10 * scale);\n  ctx.beginPath();\n  ctx.moveTo(p[0] - sz, p[1] - sz);\n  ctx.lineTo(p[0] + sz, p[1] + sz);\n  ctx.moveTo(p[0] + sz, p[1] - sz);\n  ctx.lineTo(p[0] - sz, p[1] + sz);\n  ctx.lineWidth = Math.round(8 * scale);\n  ctx.strokeStyle = '#f00';\n  ctx.stroke();\n}\nfunction drawArm(cnv, ctx, segs, tgt){\n  var pt1 = segs[0];\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#fff';\n  ctx.fillRect(0, 0, cnv.width, cnv.height);\n  ctx.beginPath();\n  ctx.moveTo(0, pt1[1]);\n  ctx.lineTo(cnv.width, pt1[1]);\n  ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n  ctx.strokeStyle = '#000';\n  ctx.stroke();\n  for (var i = 1; i < segs.length; i++){\n    var pt2 = segs[i];\n    ctx.beginPath();\n    var ang = Math.atan2(pt2[1] - pt1[1], pt2[0] - pt1[0]) + Math.PI * 0.5;\n    var dx = Math.cos(ang) * 40;\n    var dy = Math.sin(ang) * 40;\n    if (i == segs.length - 1){\n      // last element, make pointy tip\n      var ptdx = pt2[0] - pt1[0];\n      var ptdy = pt2[1] - pt1[1];\n      var ldist = Math.sqrt(ptdx * ptdx + ptdy * ptdy);\n      var pdist = Math.min(50, ldist);\n      var pti = [\n        pt1[0] + (ldist - pdist) * ptdx / ldist,\n        pt1[1] + (ldist - pdist) * ptdy / ldist\n      ];\n      ctx.moveTo(pt1[0] + dx, pt1[1] + dy);\n      ctx.lineTo(pti[0] + dx, pti[1] + dy);\n      ctx.lineTo(pt2[0], pt2[1]);\n      ctx.lineTo(pti[0] - dx, pti[1] - dy);\n      ctx.lineTo(pt1[0] - dx, pt1[1] - dy);\n    }\n    else{\n      // otherwise make a box\n      ctx.moveTo(pt1[0] + dx, pt1[1] + dy);\n      ctx.lineTo(pt2[0] + dx, pt2[1] + dy);\n      ctx.lineTo(pt2[0] - dx, pt2[1] - dy);\n      ctx.lineTo(pt1[0] - dx, pt1[1] - dy);\n    }\n    ctx.closePath();\n    ctx.strokeStyle = '#000';\n    ctx.stroke();\n    pt1 = pt2;\n  }\n  // draw joints\n  for (var i = 0; i < segs.length - 1; i++){\n    ctx.beginPath();\n    ctx.arc(segs[i][0], segs[i][1], 20, 0, Math.PI * 2);\n    ctx.strokeStyle = '#000';\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#ddf';\n    ctx.fill();\n    ctx.stroke();\n  }\n  // draw tgt\n  if (tgt !== false)\n    drawX(ctx, tgt, 1);\n}\nfunction redrawCnv1(init, mp){\n  var cnv = document.getElementById('cnv1');\n  var ctx = cnv.getContext('2d');\n  //if (init)\n  //  cnv.addEventListener('mousemove', function(e){ redrawCnv1(false, mousepos(e)); })\n  drawArm(cnv, ctx, [\n    [200, 500],\n    [200, 200],\n    [500, 100],\n    mp,\n  ],\n  [800, 200]);\n}\nredrawCnv1(true, [700, 300]);\n</script>\n<p><strong>How do you calculate the correct angle of each joint in order to hit the target?</strong></p>\n<p>This seems stupid at first – we solve this problem all day long, inside our bodies, as we reach\nfor objects and navigate the world.  But there is surprising complexity in this problem.</p>\n<p>In order to appreciate the FABRIK solution, watch the following video as different algorithms\nattempt to solve IK in 3D:</p>\n<div class=\"img flat\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tN6RQ4yrNPU#t=39\"><img src=\"/a/fabrik-algorithm-2d/video.jpg\" style=\"height: auto;\" alt=\"FABRIK Demonstration Video\" width=\"600\" height=\"453\"></a><p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tN6RQ4yrNPU#t=39\">FABRIK Demonstration Video</a></p></div>\n\n<h2 id=\"iterative-reaching\">Iterative Reaching</h2>\n<p>FABRIK’s solution to this problem is to iteratively <em>reach</em> for a target location.</p>\n<p>Let’s start with the most basic setup.</p>\n<p>Suppose there aren’t any joints, and you simply want a line of a fixed length to follow your mouse\ncursor:</p>\n<div class=\"img flat\">\n  <canvas id=\"cnv2\" width=\"1200\" height=\"600\" style=\"width: 600px; height: auto;\"></canvas><p>Use Mouse to Pull Line</p></div>\n\n<script>\nfunction reach(pt1, pt2, tgt){\n  // returns new pt1 and pt2 in the format of:\n  //   [new_pt1, new_pt2]\n  // where `new_pt1` has been moved to `tgt`\n\n  // calculate the current length\n  var c_dx = pt2[0] - pt1[0];\n  var c_dy = pt2[1] - pt1[1];\n  var c_dist = Math.sqrt(c_dx * c_dx + c_dy * c_dy);\n\n  // calculate the stretched length\n  var s_dx = pt2[0] - tgt[0];\n  var s_dy = pt2[1] - tgt[1];\n  var s_dist = Math.sqrt(s_dx * s_dx + s_dy * s_dy);\n\n  // calculate how much to scale the stretched line\n  var scale = c_dist / s_dist;\n\n  // return the result\n  return [\n    // copy the target for the new pt1\n    [tgt[0], tgt[1]],\n\n    // scale the new pt2 based on distance from target\n    [tgt[0] + s_dx * scale, tgt[1] + s_dy * scale]\n  ];\n}\nfunction drawCursor(ctx, p, scale){\n  var pts = [111, 120, 65, 120, 80, 160, 52, 174, 34, 128, 0, 165];\n  scale *= 0.3;\n  ctx.beginPath();\n  var lw = Math.round(13 * scale);\n  var lw2 = lw * 0.5;\n  ctx.moveTo(p[0] + lw2, p[1] + lw2);\n  for (var i = 0; i < pts.length; i += 2)\n    ctx.lineTo(p[0] + lw2 + pts[i] * scale, p[1] + lw2 + pts[i + 1] * scale);\n  ctx.closePath();\n  ctx.lineWidth = lw;\n  ctx.strokeStyle = '#ddd';\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#000';\n  ctx.fill();\n  ctx.stroke();\n}\nfunction drawLine(ctx, p1, p2, scale, style){\n  if (typeof style == 'undefined')\n    style = ['#000', '#ddf', '#ddf'];\n  ctx.beginPath();\n  ctx.moveTo(p1[0], p1[1]);\n  ctx.lineTo(p2[0], p2[1]);\n  ctx.lineWidth = Math.round(10 * scale);\n  ctx.strokeStyle = style[0];\n  ctx.stroke();\n  function circ(p, col){\n    ctx.beginPath();\n    ctx.arc(p[0], p[1], Math.round(10 * scale), 0, Math.PI * 2);\n    ctx.lineWidth = Math.round(2 * scale);\n    ctx.strokeStyle = style[0];\n    ctx.fillStyle = col;\n    ctx.fill();\n    ctx.stroke();\n  }\n  circ(p1, style[1]);\n  circ(p2, style[2]);\n}\nfunction redrawCnv2(init, mp){\n  var cnv = document.getElementById('cnv2');\n  var ctx = cnv.getContext('2d');\n  if (init){\n    // inject global line object\n    window.cnv2_line = { pt1: [500, 250], pt2: [700, 350], auto: true, ang: 0 };\n    function tick(){\n      if (!window.cnv2_line.auto)\n        return;\n      var ang = window.cnv2_line.ang;\n      window.cnv2_line.ang = (ang + 0.025) % (Math.PI * 2);\n      redrawCnv2(false, [\n        600 + 500 * Math.cos(ang * 3),\n        300 + 200 * Math.sin(ang * 2)\n      ]);\n      setTimeout(tick, 50);\n    }\n    tick();\n    cnv.addEventListener('mousemove', function(e){\n      window.cnv2_line.auto = false;\n      redrawCnv2(false, mousepos(e));\n    });\n    return;\n  }\n\n  var line = window.cnv2_line;\n  var r = reach(line.pt1, line.pt2, mp);\n  line.pt1 = r[0];\n  line.pt2 = r[1];\n\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#fff';\n  ctx.fillRect(0, 0, cnv.width, cnv.height);\n  drawLine(ctx, line.pt1, line.pt2, 1);\n  if (line.auto) // draw fake mouse cursor\n    drawCursor(ctx, mp, 1);\n}\nredrawCnv2(true);\n</script>\n<p><em>Reaching</em>, according to FABRIK, consists of:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Given a line and a target…</li>\n<li>Set the line’s head point to the target, stretching the line</li>\n<li>Slide the line’s tail point along the new stretched line to fix the length</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Let’s look at this visually.</p>\n<p>Given a line and a target:</p>\n<div class=\"img flat\">\n  <canvas id=\"cnv3\" width=\"1000\" height=\"500\" style=\"width: 500px; height: auto;\"></canvas></div>\n\n<script>\nfunction redrawCnv3(){\n  var cnv = document.getElementById('cnv3');\n  var ctx = cnv.getContext('2d');\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#fff';\n  ctx.fillRect(0, 0, cnv.width, cnv.height);\n  drawLine(ctx, [140, 400], [400, 100], 3);\n  drawX(ctx, [800, 300], 3);\n  drawCursor(ctx, [800, 300], 3);\n}\nredrawCnv3();\n</script>\n<p>Set the line’s head to the target:</p>\n<div class=\"img flat\">\n  <canvas id=\"cnv4\" width=\"1000\" height=\"500\" style=\"width: 500px; height: auto;\"></canvas></div>\n\n<script>\nfunction redrawCnv4(){\n  var cnv = document.getElementById('cnv4');\n  var ctx = cnv.getContext('2d');\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#fff';\n  ctx.fillRect(0, 0, cnv.width, cnv.height);\n  drawLine(ctx, [140, 400], [400, 100], 3, ['#aaa', '#fff', '#fff']);\n  drawLine(ctx, [140, 400], [800, 300], 3);\n  drawCursor(ctx, [800, 300], 3);\n}\nredrawCnv4();\n</script>\n<p>Notice that this <em>stretches</em> the line.  We fix that by sliding the tail <em>along the new line</em>:</p>\n<div class=\"img flat\">\n  <canvas id=\"cnv5\" width=\"1000\" height=\"500\" style=\"width: 500px; height: auto;\"></canvas></div>\n\n<script>\nfunction drawArrow(ctx, p1, p2, col, scale){\n  ctx.beginPath();\n  ctx.moveTo(p1[0], p1[1]);\n  ctx.lineTo(p2[0], p2[1]);\n  var ang = Math.atan2(p2[1] - p1[1], p2[0] - p1[0]);\n  var spr = 2.5;\n  var len = Math.round(15 * scale);\n  ctx.moveTo(p2[0] + Math.cos(ang + spr) * len, p2[1] + Math.sin(ang + spr) * len);\n  ctx.lineTo(p2[0], p2[1]);\n  ctx.lineTo(p2[0] + Math.cos(ang - spr) * len, p2[1] + Math.sin(ang - spr) * len);\n  ctx.lineWidth = Math.round(4 * scale);\n  ctx.strokeStyle = col;\n  ctx.stroke();\n}\nfunction redrawCnv5(){\n  var cnv = document.getElementById('cnv5');\n  var ctx = cnv.getContext('2d');\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#fff';\n  ctx.fillRect(0, 0, cnv.width, cnv.height);\n  drawLine(ctx, [140, 400], [400, 100], 3, ['#aaa', '#fff', '#fff']);\n  drawLine(ctx, [140, 400], [800, 300], 3, ['#aaa', '#fff', '#fff']);\n  drawLine(ctx, [407, 359], [800, 300], 3);\n  var dx = 5, dy = 60;\n  drawArrow(ctx, [140+dx, 400+dy], [407+dx, 359+dy], '#f00', 3);\n  drawCursor(ctx, [800, 300], 3);\n}\nredrawCnv5();\n</script>\n<p>Let’s look at some code:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" class=\"chroma\"><code class=\"language-javascript\" data-lang=\"javascript\"><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"kd\">function</span> <span class=\"nx\">reach</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">head</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nx\">tail</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span><span class=\"p\">){</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"c1\">// returns new head and tail in the format of:\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>  <span class=\"c1\">//   [new_head, new_tail]\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>  <span class=\"c1\">// where `new_head` has been moved to `tgt`\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"c1\">// calculate the current length\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>  <span class=\"c1\">// (in practice, this should be calculated once and saved,\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>  <span class=\"c1\">//  not re-calculated every time `reach` is called)\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>  <span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">c_dx</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">tail</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">x</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"nx\">head</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">x</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">c_dy</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">tail</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">y</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"nx\">head</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">y</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">c_dist</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nb\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">sqrt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">c_dx</span> <span class=\"o\">*</span> <span class=\"nx\">c_dx</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"nx\">c_dy</span> <span class=\"o\">*</span> <span class=\"nx\">c_dy</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"c1\">// calculate the stretched length\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>  <span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">s_dx</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">tail</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">x</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">x</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">s_dy</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">tail</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">y</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">y</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">s_dist</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nb\">Math</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">sqrt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">s_dx</span> <span class=\"o\">*</span> <span class=\"nx\">s_dx</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"nx\">s_dy</span> <span class=\"o\">*</span> <span class=\"nx\">s_dy</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"c1\">// calculate how much to scale the stretched line\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>  <span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">scale</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">c_dist</span> <span class=\"o\">/</span> <span class=\"nx\">s_dist</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"c1\">// return the result\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>  <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">    <span class=\"c1\">// copy the target for the new head\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>    <span class=\"p\">{</span> <span class=\"nx\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">x</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nx\">y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">y</span> <span class=\"p\">},</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">    <span class=\"c1\">// scale the new tail based on distance from target\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>    <span class=\"p\">{</span> <span class=\"nx\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">x</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"nx\">s_dx</span> <span class=\"o\">*</span> <span class=\"nx\">scale</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nx\">y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">y</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"nx\">s_dy</span> <span class=\"o\">*</span> <span class=\"nx\">scale</span> <span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"p\">];</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>This should be fairly straight-forward, but there is one important property to notice:</p>\n<p>This function <em>always</em> succeeds.  The line will <em>always</em> be moved so that it touches the target.</p>\n<h2 id=\"making-it-iterative\">Making it Iterative</h2>\n<p>How can we make the process iterative?  I.e., instead of pulling around a single line, how can we\npull along a <em>chain</em> of lines?</p>\n<div class=\"img flat\">\n  <canvas id=\"cnv6\" width=\"1200\" height=\"600\" style=\"width: 600px; height: auto;\"></canvas><p>Use Mouse to Pull Chain</p></div>\n\n<script>\nfunction redrawCnv6(init, mp){\n  var cnv = document.getElementById('cnv6');\n  var ctx = cnv.getContext('2d');\n  if (init){\n    // inject global line object\n    window.cnv6_segs = {\n      segs: [[500, 250], [600, 300], [700, 350], [800, 400], [900, 450]],\n      auto: true, ang: 0\n    };\n    function tick(){\n      if (!window.cnv6_segs.auto)\n        return;\n      var ang = window.cnv6_segs.ang;\n      window.cnv6_segs.ang = (ang + 0.025) % (Math.PI * 2);\n      redrawCnv6(false, [\n        600 + 500 * Math.cos(ang * 3),\n        300 + 200 * Math.sin(ang * 2)\n      ]);\n      setTimeout(tick, 50);\n    }\n    tick();\n    cnv.addEventListener('mousemove', function(e){\n      window.cnv6_segs.auto = false;\n      redrawCnv6(false, mousepos(e));\n    });\n    return;\n  }\n\n  var segs = window.cnv6_segs.segs;\n\n  var tgt = mp;\n  for (var i = 0; i < segs.length - 1; i++){\n    var r = reach(segs[i], segs[i + 1], tgt);\n    segs[i] = r[0];\n    tgt = r[1];\n  }\n  segs[segs.length - 1] = tgt;\n\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#fff';\n  ctx.fillRect(0, 0, cnv.width, cnv.height);\n  for (var i = 0; i < segs.length - 1; i++)\n    drawLine(ctx, segs[i], segs[i + 1], 1);\n  if (window.cnv6_segs.auto) // draw fake mouse cursor\n    drawCursor(ctx, mp, 1);\n}\nredrawCnv6(true);\n</script>\n<p>It’s quite ingenious:</p>\n<p>The act of sliding the tail along the line <em>can itself be a reach</em>.</p>\n<p>Think about it.  We have all the ingredients.</p>\n<p>To perform a reach, we need a line (head + tail), and a target location.  Well, in a chain, the tail\nof one segment is the head of another segment.  For each segment, we simply perform a reach with the\nnew target, until we run out of segments – then we slide the final tail to the target:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" class=\"chroma\"><code class=\"language-javascript\" data-lang=\"javascript\"><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\">// initialize target\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span><span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">mousePosition</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\">// for each segment (except the last one)\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span><span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">i</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span> <span class=\"nx\">i</span> <span class=\"o\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">length</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span> <span class=\"nx\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">){</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"c1\">// perform a reach for this segment\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>  <span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">r</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">reach</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">i</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">i</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"c1\">// update this node\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>  <span class=\"c1\">// (`r[0]` is guaranteed to be the same point as `tgt`)\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>  <span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">i</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">];</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"c1\">// update the target, so the next segment's head\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>  <span class=\"c1\">// targets this segments new tail\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span>  <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">];</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\">// for the last segment, move it to the target\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span><span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">length</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id=\"forward-and-backward\">Forward and Backward</h2>\n<p>We haven’t <em>quite</em> made a robot arm though, have we?</p>\n<p>A robot arm doesn’t move around freely like a chain – it’s fixed at the base.</p>\n<p>The last insight of FABRIK is that since we are guaranteed the head of the chain will always reach\nits target, we can perform the iterative reach <em>in reverse</em> to ensure that the base of the arm will\nalways stay fixed.</p>\n<p>Said another way:</p>\n<p>First we perform the iterative reach like normal, so the head is guaranteed to be touching the\ntarget.  Then we perform the iterative reach in reverse, so that the tail is guaranteed to be\ntouching the base.</p>\n<p>And <em>that</em> gives us an arm:</p>\n<div class=\"img flat\">\n  <canvas id=\"cnv7\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\" style=\"width: 600px; height: auto;\"></canvas><p>Working Robot Arm</p></div>\n\n<script>\nfunction redrawCnv7(init, mp){\n  var cnv = document.getElementById('cnv7');\n  var ctx = cnv.getContext('2d');\n  if (init){\n    // inject global line object\n    window.cnv7_segs = {\n      segs: [\n        [700, 500],\n        [500, 300],\n        [200, 400],\n        [200, 700]\n      ],\n      auto: true, ang: 0\n    };\n    function tick(){\n      if (!window.cnv7_segs.auto)\n        return;\n      var ang = window.cnv7_segs.ang;\n      window.cnv7_segs.ang = (ang + 0.025) % (Math.PI * 2);\n      redrawCnv7(false, [\n        600 + 500 * Math.cos(ang * 3),\n        300 + 200 * Math.sin(ang * 2)\n      ]);\n      setTimeout(tick, 50);\n    }\n    tick();\n    cnv.addEventListener('mousemove', function(e){\n      window.cnv7_segs.auto = false;\n      redrawCnv7(false, mousepos(e));\n    });\n    return;\n  }\n\n  var segs = window.cnv7_segs.segs;\n\n  var base = segs[segs.length - 1];\n  var tgt = mp;\n  for (var i = 0; i < segs.length - 1; i++){\n    var r = reach(segs[i], segs[i + 1], tgt);\n    segs[i] = r[0];\n    tgt = r[1];\n  }\n  segs[segs.length - 1] = tgt;\n\n  tgt = base;\n  for (var i = segs.length - 1; i > 0; i--){\n    var r = reach(segs[i], segs[i - 1], tgt);\n    segs[i] = r[0];\n    tgt = r[1];\n  }\n  segs[0] = tgt;\n\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#fff';\n  ctx.fillRect(0, 0, cnv.width, cnv.height);\n  var segs_rev = segs.concat();\n  segs_rev.reverse();\n  drawArm(cnv, ctx, segs_rev, false);\n  if (window.cnv7_segs.auto) // draw fake mouse cursor\n    drawCursor(ctx, mp, 1);\n}\nredrawCnv7(true);\n</script>\n<p>Here’s the code:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" class=\"chroma\"><code class=\"language-javascript\" data-lang=\"javascript\"><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\">// save the fixed base location\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span><span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">base</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">length</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">];</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\">// perform the iterative reach in the forward direction\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\">// (same as before)\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span><span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">mousePosition</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">i</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span> <span class=\"nx\">i</span> <span class=\"o\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">length</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span> <span class=\"nx\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">){</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">r</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">reach</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">i</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">i</span> <span class=\"o\">+</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">i</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">];</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">];</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">length</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\">// at this point, our base has moved from its original\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\">// location... so perform the iterative reach in reverse,\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\">// with the target set to the initial base location\n</span></span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"c1\"></span><span class=\"nx\">tgt</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">base</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">i</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">length</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span> <span class=\"nx\">i</span> <span class=\"o\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span> <span class=\"nx\">i</span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"p\">){</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"kd\">var</span> <span class=\"nx\">r</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">reach</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">i</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">i</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">i</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">];</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\">  <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">r</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">];</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"cl\"><span class=\"nx\">segments</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">]</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"nx\">tgt</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id=\"conclusion\">Conclusion</h2>\n<p>It’s quite amazing that such a simple concept – a stretched reach – has turned into solving the\ncomplex and puzzling inverse kinematics problem.</p>\n<p>There are a lot of ways to extend this algorithm too.</p>\n<p>Moving into 3D complicates it because orientation of the segments matter, but by tweaking the\n<code>reach</code> function, it can be made to work.</p>\n<p>Adding constraints like fixed range of motion over a joint is possible too, but requires thought\nabout where to enforce the constraints during the iterative process.</p>\n<p>Moving objects other than lines is possible too (i.e., rigid triangles), if you can break down the\nobjects into lines, and traverse the heirarchy correctly while iterating.</p>\n<p>The important part is understanding the core idea, which I hope is clear now.  Go forth, experiment,\nand have fun!</p><h2 class=\"foot\"><span>Tags:</span>\n      <a href=\"/t/2d/\">2d,</a>\n      <a href=\"/t/algorithm/\">Algorithm,</a>\n      <a href=\"/t/javascript/\">Javascript,</a>\n      <a href=\"/t/heuristic/\">Heuristic</a><br><br><a href=\"/all\">View All Posts</a>\n    </h2>\n  </article></main>\n      <aside class=\"spacer\"></aside>\n    </div>\n    <footer>\n      <span class=\"no-print\">XML:</span>\n      <a href=\"/rss.xml\" class=\"no-print\">RSS</a>\n      <span class=\"no-print\">|</span>\n      <a href=\"/sitemap.xml\" class=\"no-print\">Sitemap</a><br class=\"no-print\">\n      <span>© Copyright 2026</span>\n      <a href=\"/who\">Sean Connelly</a><span>, All Rights Reserved</span>\n    </footer>\n  \n\n</body></html>",
